{"base_rate":0.47291941875825627,"brier":0.24086036988110965,"bss":0.033724016045700744,"bss_hi":0.12897536848962163,"bss_lo":-0.07722047981642081,"chart":{"base":[675.2,219.4],"fp":[451.0,224.2],"lead":"62,135.9 272,127.6 482,122.9 692,108.6","note":{"base":"skill 0.03 — higher than 7% of cities","fp":"low end +21pp, high end +21pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.2 °C — better than 2% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 25%; promised 93% → rained 72%"},"rel":"82.9,358.7 330,282.1 649.2,156.2"},"country":"GB","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.19449141347424045,"ess":396.2637980806686,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Leicester</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Leicester rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>75%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>19%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSUTTON BONINGTON, 23.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.03, ranked 124 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(117&ndash;130) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>221</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>79%</td><td class='num'><b>61%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>75%</b></td><td class='num'>228</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Leicester</b> <span class=\"muted\">GB</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.03</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>117&ndash;130\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Leicester &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Leicester\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><t